    {
      "id": 99337,
      "name": "Kharnel",
      "username": "Kharnel",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/kharnel/{size}/1984_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-04-16T23:37:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>You know how the Mobile Defense Platform is a pretty tame environment overall? Oh, maybe you get plinked a few times, but mostly you just let it do its thing and build up?</p><p>Well, I was playing Cosmic Omnitron last night, and there were seven environment cards in play when Terraforming hit. So, seven villain cards plus an extra one for each drone (he was in Dropship mode) resulted in 11 villain cards, two of which were Electro Pulse Explosives.</p><p>I actually pulled this one out by the skin of my teeth and killed him before they could go off, but it made me very conscious of the environment's interaction with ol' \"pushover\" Omnitron.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:27:16.628Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
